From 2022c2c09f1d287bd9d253dc5d3decb696fa101a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AdrianProk <Prokopczyk.Adrian@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:50:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] 3DS: Use the normal top screen mode in the standalone
 build (MAUSJAGD_PORT)

The backend switches the top screen to the 800px wide mode. The
standalone build shows the game 1:1 or scaled on the top screen, so the
half-width pixels bring no gain there, and the emulator Azahar shows
only the left half of the wide framebuffer, stretched to the full
width. The standalone build now keeps the normal 400x240 mode, which
the backend already supports.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 backends/platform/3ds/main.cpp | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/backends/platform/3ds/main.cpp b/backends/platform/3ds/main.cpp
index df87586a0a..c5ef979830 100644
--- a/backends/platform/3ds/main.cpp
+++ b/backends/platform/3ds/main.cpp
@@ -53,7 +53,15 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[]) {
 	// 800px wide top screen is not available on old 2DS systems
 	u8 systemModel = 0;
 	CFGU_GetSystemModel(&systemModel);
+#ifdef MAUSJAGD_PORT
+	// Standalone build: normal 400x240 top screen. The game is shown 1:1 or
+	// scaled there, so the 800px mode with its half-width pixels brings no gain,
+	// and emulators like Azahar show only its left half, stretched.
+	gfxSetWide(false);
+	(void)systemModel;
+#else
 	gfxSetWide(systemModel != SYSTEM_MODEL_2DS);
+#endif
 
 	romfsInit();
 	osSetSpeedupEnable(true);
